<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Kharan State</h1><p class="st-meta">1697 CE – 1955 CE (approx.) · capital Kharan</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Baloch chiefdom of the deserts of western Balochistan, ruled by the Nausherwani family and long a feudatory of Kalat.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Kharan was ruled by the Nausherwani <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baloch">Baloch</a>, who claimed descent from Persian nobles. The register dates its founding to 1697. Through much of its history it acknowledged the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khanate-of-kalat">Khanate of Kalat</a>, while contending for independence.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The chiefs ruled a vast, arid territory of sand desert and scattered oases, with a small nomadic and farming population. The British treated Kharan as a feudatory of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khanate-of-kalat">Kalat</a> but dealt with its chiefs directly.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Kharan acceded to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/islamic-republic-of-pakistan">Pakistan</a> in 1948, joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/baluchistan-states-union">Baluchistan States Union</a> in 1952 and was absorbed into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-pakistan">West Pakistan</a> in 1955. It is now a district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balochistan">Balochistan</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kharan-state.jpg" alt="Kharan State" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Mysid · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_State_of_Kharan.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1697 CE – 1955 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kharan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Balochi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/pakistan">Pakistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kharan</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/at